{#
  Layout: same as the OpenCart 4 core payment extensions (bank_transfer, cod): a 'text-end' block
  and the id 'button-confirm'. Do not put the button in a floated element: the container of a
  floated element has no height, so the next element on the confirm page can cover the button.

  The button is a link with an inline onclick, and it does not need jQuery or a <script> block:
  - normal click and click without JavaScript: the browser opens the href,
  - $('#button-confirm').trigger('click') from a one page checkout: jQuery calls the onclick,
  - confirm HTML added with innerHTML (scripts do not run) or jQuery loaded at the end of the page: works.
#}
{% if description %}
  <div class="blockonomics-description mb-3">{{ description }}</div>
{% endif %}
<div class="text-end">
  <a href="{{ url_redirect }}" id="button-confirm" class="btn btn-primary" role="button" onclick="window.location.href = this.href; return false;">{{ button_confirm }}</a>
</div>
